Done. Audit found one real bug: `setPeerConnChip()` in `ui/live.js` set the trio/2v2 peer-chip tooltip (`title`) to the raw `RTCPeerConnection` state string (e.g. `"completed"`, `"checking"`) instead of the already-computed localized label, bypassing i18n entirely while the visible chip text was correctly translated. Fixed with a 1-line change reusing the existing `label` variable. The main `#conn-chip` was already correctly localized, and static hardcoded HTML titles are unreachable (elements start hidden and get their titles overwritten by JS before being shown), so those were left alone. `node --check` passes. RESULT written to `tasks/admin-queue/done/147-web-conn-status-chip-label-RESULT.md`.
